; Sprites: profile critter (4 frames), hooded figure (4 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B800+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Frames 0-3 look like an animal in profile with a pointed tip at the
; top; frames 4-7 look like an upright hooded figure whose arms go up and down. Entities that use all eight frames show
; one while moving left and the other while moving right (bit 7 of entity byte +0). Used by entity definitions $20 $21
; $22 $23 in rooms $02 $12 $15 $2E.
@label=SpritesCritterHooded
